<title>USA: American Pad Q4 oper shr $0.36 vs loss.</title>
<headline>American Pad Q4 oper shr $0.36 vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMERICAN PAD &amp; PAPER CO.</p>
<p>			 (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					Three Months Ended December 31</p>
<p>				 1996     1995	   1996	1995</p>
<p>				   Actual		    Pro forma</p>
<p> Net Sales	     $176,046 $111,151	$176,046 $168,218</p>
<p> Gross Profit	    40,914   24,049	  40,914   35,118</p>
<p>Operating Income</p>
<p>	     (Loss)	26,447  (13,345)(1)    27,696   20,338</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>  extraordinary item   10,466  (12,348)    11,340    8,073(2)</p>
<p> Net Income(Loss)	10,466  (22,000)	 11,340  (1,081)</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>Common Shares</p>
<p>   Outstanding	   29,607   29,607	  29,607   29,607</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss)</p>
<p>per share before</p>
<p>   extraordinary item    0.36  ( 0.42)	    0.38     0.27</p>
<p>(1) Operating results for the fourth quarter of 1995 included a non- recurring compensation charge of $27,632 in connection with the acquisition of Williamhouse and the Company's recapitalization. (2) The pro forma net income for the three months ended December 31, 1995 has been adjusted to reflect an annualized effective tax rate of 36.1%, the Company's pro forma effective tax rate for all of 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
